<item>
            <title>[ZEPPELIN-1963] Cron job doesn&apos;t have executing user by default</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/ZEPPELIN-1963</link>
                <project id="12316221" key="ZEPPELIN">Zeppelin</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Cron jobs have field for executing user, but by default it&apos;s empty. so there&apos;s no way to know who set the cron job, and during save the anonymous subject is passed, however in reality there was user who set the job. &lt;/p&gt;</description>
